<title>JAPAN: General Sekiyu Sakai topper to close in May, June.</title>
<headline>General Sekiyu Sakai topper to close in May, June.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Sekiyu KK said on Thursday that it plans to shut down the 156,000 barrels-per-day crude distillation unit at its refinery at Sakai in Osaka, western Japan, for 36 days from May 14 for routine maintenance checks.</p>
<p>General Sekiyu is owned 49 percent by Exxon Corp.</p>
